{
  "analysis": "Now let's examine the remaining binary files:
- `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`
- `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`
- `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`
- `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`
- `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`

Let's use `strings` or python scripts on these files.",
  "plan": "Run strings on OBJECTS.DATA, System.evtx, lsass.dmp, srv.sys, and SECURITY.bak.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings /disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA | grep -E -i \"powershell|event|filter|consumer|binding|select|c2|http|enc|mssecsvc|lsass|198\\.|203\\.\" | head -n 30\necho \"=== strings System.evtx ===\"\nstrings /disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx | head -n 30\necho \"=== strings lsass.dmp ===\"\nstrings /disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp | head -n 30\necho \"=== strings srv.sys ===\"\nstrings /disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys | head -n 30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "`/sas` is writable! But wait, let's re-read the prompt on `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`:
Prompt says:
\"`/sas/handoff/` — a pre-filled change ticket with stale/incorrect entries to reconcile in place, a findings JSON schema, and an incident intake form. Map your on-disk findings to the advisory's ATT&CK claims, and correct the change ticket against your own evidence rather than trusting it.\"

Wait! Reconcile in place? Does that mean we should update `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` OR put the reconciled change ticket in `remediation-plan.md` OR both?
Let's check `touch /sas/handoff/test.txt` succeeded! So `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` can be modified in place as well as including it in `remediation-plan.md`. Let's clean up test.txt first.",
  "plan": "Remove `/sas/handoff/test.txt`.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -f /sas/handoff/test.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

